<title>INDIA: India to release extra wheat, rice in January.</title>
<headline>India to release extra wheat, rice in January.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Indian government will release 912,000 tonnes of wheat in January 1997 to the states and the union territories for sale under the public distribution system, the United News of India (UNI) said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>UNI was quoting a Food Ministry statement that said 844,000 tonnes had been released under the public distribution system in December 1996.</p>
<p>The rice allocation for January 1997 has also been marginally increased to 1.28 million tonnes, against 1.26 million in December, UNI said.</p>
<p>-- New Delhi newsroom +91-11-301 2024</p>
